In addition to varying the angle of the lower jet (θ2), we consider a range of flow conditions by controlling the pressure of the upper (P1 = 0–0.1 MPa) and lower (P2 = 0–0.4 MPa) jets independently, by which we achieve the exit velocity of the upper and lower jets up
